[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Queen's Gambit"]
[Variation "Queen's Gambit Declined: Chigorin Defense, Main Line"]
[ECO "D07"]
[Character "positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "bishop-pair-for-structure"]
[Kind "sideline"]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 Nc6 3. Nf3 { Develops and guards e5, so Black's knight on c6 has no easy way to push ...e5. } 3... Bg4
( 3... e5 4. Nxe5 Nxe5 5. dxe5 d4 6. g3 )
4. cxd5 { Takes the pawn now, because the bishop on g4 leaves the knight on f3 exposed. } 4... Bxf3
5. gxf3 { Recaptures towards the centre, which gives up the pawn structure but opens the g-file and keeps White's bishop pair. } 5... Qxd5
6. e3 { Opens the bishop on f1 and guards d4. } 6... e5
7. Nc3 { Hits the queen, so Black must spend another move on it. } 7... Bb4
8. Bd2 { Unpins the knight on c3 and gets ready to castle long. Plan: use the two bishops, castle queenside and play on the open g-file. } *
